  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Inverting summing amplifier"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Several inputs $V_1, V_2, V_3$ are applied through resistors $R_1, R_2, R_3$ to the inverting terminal, with feedback resistor $R_f$. The inverting terminal is a virtual ground, so the input currents $V_1/R_1$, $V_2/R_2$, $V_3/R_3$ add and all flow through $R_f$. Hence $V_o = -R_f(V_1/R_1 + V_2/R_2 + V_3/R_3)$. If all resistors equal $R_f$, $V_o = -(V_1 + V_2 + V_3)$; if $R_f = R/3$, the output is minus the average. With unequal resistors it is a scaling (weighted) adder, as used in audio mixers and D/A converters."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Vo = −Rf(V1/R1 + V2/R2 + V3/R3)"
    },
    {
     "en": "All R = Rf: Vo = −(V1 + V2 + V3)"
    },
    {
     "en": "Rf = R/n: averager"
    },
    {
     "en": "Uses: audio mixer, DAC"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "In a summing amplifier the input currents add at the virtual ground. With equal resistors the output is minus the sum of the inputs.",
    "kn": "ಸಮ್ಮಿಂಗ್ ವರ್ಧಕದಲ್ಲಿ ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಪ್ರವಾಹಗಳು ವರ್ಚುವಲ್ ಗ್ರೌಂಡ್‌ನಲ್ಲಿ ಕೂಡುತ್ತವೆ. ಸಮಾನ ರೋಧಕಗಳಿದ್ದರೆ ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್ = −(ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್‌ಗಳ ಮೊತ್ತ)."
   },
   "formula": "V_o = -R_f\\left(\\frac{V_1}{R_1} + \\frac{V_2}{R_2} + \\frac{V_3}{R_3}\\right)"
  },
