  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Subtractor (difference amplifier)"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "In a subtractor, $V_1$ is applied through $R_1$ to the inverting input (with $R_f$ in feedback) and $V_2$ through $R_2$ to the non-inverting input, which has $R_3$ to ground. When $R_f/R_1 = R_3/R_2$, $V_o = (R_f/R_1)(V_2 - V_1)$. With all four resistors equal, $V_o = V_2 - V_1$. By superposition: $V_1$ alone gives $-V_1$; $V_2$ alone is halved by the divider and then multiplied by 2, giving $+V_2$."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "All four R equal: Vo = V2 − V1"
    },
    {
     "en": "General: Vo = (Rf/R1)(V2 − V1) with matched ratios"
    },
    {
     "en": "Prove by superposition"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "With four equal resistors the difference amplifier gives V2 minus V1, where V1 goes to the inverting input.",
    "kn": "ನಾಲ್ಕು ಸಮಾನ ರೋಧಕಗಳಿರುವ ಸಬ್‌ಟ್ರ್ಯಾಕ್ಟರ್ Vo = V2 − V1 ನೀಡುತ್ತದೆ; V1 ಇನ್ವರ್ಟಿಂಗ್ ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್‌ಗೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತದೆ."
   },
   "formula": "V_o = V_2 - V_1 \\quad (\\text{all resistors equal})"
  },
